Only my second and with an archaeologist no less!

I need that program that gives you a nice list of everything but until
I get and implement a copy I'll just give you it in brief.

I've been wanting to ascend an Archaeologist for a while now, mainly
because they're an inbetweeny class and they have a bit of everything,
intrinsic speed, expert in pick axe (and hence dwavish mattock), and
they're powers not terrible so they can cast a few decent spells.
They seem like a good choice but the early games a killer and until
you get your stats up and find a dwavish mattock, (of which I found
about 4 all game 3 of which went rusty), it's damn hard.

Pets are your friend though. and mine was no exception, handily
helping me rob a couple of shops on the way to the mines, got some
protection at exp 1 and I was away.  Most of it was fairly straight
forward, did sokoban early on and then back down the mines to bless a
flint stone that I carried around with me for ages :)  Stupidly I only
found out when I rubbed it on my touchstone by accident... I didn't
know you could identify stones with your touchstone too.... well...
you live and learn I guess... Found a Bag of holding in the mines
somewhere and a amulet of reflection in sokoban. Aces! I also found a
bones file from a valkyrie who was wearing suspicous gloves that
turned out to be gloves of dexterity and also a sword .. Excaliber!
Which I was restricted in... bummer.

So back down the mines and then onward... Bit of luck in that there
was an alter on the same level as the sokoban stairs and then another
on about level twenty something a level above medusa.  Handy
placement!

Did a bit of alter camping, just walked around for what seemed like
ages to find any potions to convert to holy water, and scrolls to
blank and write enchant armours on.  Was finally awarded with
Trollsbane, Sunsword, and finally Grayswandir! Yay! Just what I'd been
waiting for all along.  Bumped it up to +5 then did medusa and the
castle.

At this point I was carrying Grayswandir in hand, alternative weapon
was a dwarvish mattock (rusty) and I had Excaliber +2 in my BoH.
(Excaliber was now unrestricted as I'd been awarded sunsword) So I
took Excaliber out and read a scroll of enchant weapon.  "Grayswandir
vibrates rapidly and then evaporates" or words to that effect.  Boobs!

I used my last wish from my wand of wishing (from the castle) on Frost
brand to give me a bit of ummph in the finale and then down into hell.

I actually don't find this bit as boring as everyone makes out, of
course I had magc mapping at this point which obviously helps
alot.....

Killed the demons and stuff no problem, the worst bit was when I
killed Rodney, picked up his corpse along with the amulet and promptly
forgot I had jut taken of my ring of levitation and dumped myself in
his moat.  Fortunately I survived but I dropped his corpse, the amulet
and my beloved frost brand in the briney waters.  I had to go up ten
levels back to the alter and find a wand of cold 0:3 go back down
freeze everything and dig it up again with my mattock (which was +0 as
I had had a run in with a disenchanter).

It was tense but with an armour class of -36 you're not going to be in
too much trouble, I did a bit of nurse dancing before hell just to
make sure too.  And genocided just about everything I could think of.

Purple worms as pets are great.  They must have killed Rodney about 4
or 5 times on the way up.  The planes were fairly easy, found a scroll
of gold detection on the plane of earth which helped as I hadn't got
any.  Just had to search the hard way for the other portals.

First alter I came too was lawful, job done.

